WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:04.790
Not long after The Twilight Saga concluded,
Summit Entertainment geared up for its next

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:07.250
young adult franchise: Ender's Game.

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:11.139
Based on the Orson Scott Card novel of the
same name, Ender's Game was envisioned as

00:00:11.139 --> 00:00:15.519
the first in a series of new sci-fi films—after
all, there's a ton of written material to

00:00:15.519 --> 00:00:19.490
draw from—but the series got canned long
before its completion.

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:22.630
Here's why we never got to see an Ender's
Game sequel.

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:23.849
Box office bomb

00:00:23.849 --> 00:00:27.320
Hollywood is a business—people tend to forget
that sometimes.

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:30.929
Studio executives would love to make whatever
movies they want, but they have to make sure

00:00:30.929 --> 00:00:33.210
they'll make their money back … and then
some.

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:39.079
So when Ender's Game grossed a mere $125.5
million worldwide against a production budget

00:00:39.079 --> 00:00:43.850
of $110 million, that showed Lionsgate that
audiences weren't willing to put up with an

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:45.180
Ender's Game franchise.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:48.649
Variety called it one of the biggest box office
bombs of the year.

00:00:48.649 --> 00:00:53.469
With that kind of response, few studios would
be willing to jump onto a sequel.

00:00:53.469 --> 00:00:54.469
Boycott

00:00:54.469 --> 00:00:58.050
There are countless reasons why a movie would
flop at the box office, but for this particular

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:02.870
film, an argument can be made that Orson Scott
Card's views on homosexuality and the legalization

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:07.110
of same-sex marriage led a number of people,
especially those who were on the fence about

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:10.180
seeing Ender's Game, to boycott the movie
altogether.

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:13.900
It's impossible to say how much of an impact
the boycott had on the movie's box office

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:18.550
take, but there's no denying that in a politically
charged climate, any negative press against

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:21.240
a film like Ender's Game couldn't have helped.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:22.350
Budget constraints

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:26.610
Budget constraints are an ordinary occurrence
in Hollywood, but it's almost never a good

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:27.840
thing when it happens.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:32.490
For instance, Twentieth Century Fox kept the
budget low for James Mangold's Logan because

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:36.810
the director and Hugh Jackman wanted the film
to be rated R. While that ended up working

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:40.980
in their favor, a studio usually constrains
a movie's budget if it doesn't seem like the

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:43.260
film will be as successful as initially hoped.

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:46.110
That rings true for the would-be Ender's Game
sequel.

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:50.930
The first movie had a production budget of
$110 million, a fairly typical amount for

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:54.850
a sci-fi flick, but the sequel might have
seen that number dip below the $100 million

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:56.000
mark.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.220
Director Gavin Hood originally wanted to film
the first and second movies back to back,

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.270
but Lionsgate wasn't up for that much of a
gamble.

00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:06.930
Hood said: "It's a pity on many levels because
that cast was all there, the sets were all

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:09.890
there, we should've shot the two movies back-to-back."

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:11.760
A tired trend

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:15.940
Before superhero movies fully took over Hollywood,
each studio was attempting to launch its own

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:20.290
young adult franchise to snag some of the
success of Twilight, The Hunger Games, and

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:21.290
Harry Potter.

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:25.370
Some were successful, but most weren't, and
at this point, young adult adaptations are

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:29.280
a tired trend that audiences no longer seem
interested in paying for.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:34.090
Beautiful Creatures flopped, as did The Mortal
Instruments, and even initially successful

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:38.810
YA franchises like the Divergent series suffered
insanely diminishing returns.

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:43.090
Young adult adaptations can be successful
if budgets are kept low and if the movies

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:44.510
are marketed properly.

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:48.079
Unfortunately, every studio wants to believe
they're sitting on a gold mine, so they go

00:02:48.079 --> 00:02:52.299
full-steam ahead with the first installment,
which, in the case of Ender's Game, leaves

00:02:52.299 --> 00:02:54.879
little room for expansion in the sequel.

00:02:54.879 --> 00:02:56.349
Aged out

00:02:56.349 --> 00:03:00.900
As Gavin Hood explained to Hypable, the proposed
film sequel to Ender's Game would have been

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:05.010
been based on Ender's Shadow, which takes
place concurrently with the first book.

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:08.969
So if the studio really wanted to adapt that
story, it would have made more sense to film

00:03:08.969 --> 00:03:12.099
back-to-back, as Gavin Hood originally wanted
to do.

00:03:12.099 --> 00:03:16.709
Several years have passed, and now Asa Butterfield
and Hailee Steinfeld are far older than their

00:03:16.709 --> 00:03:18.769
pre-teen characters in the books.

00:03:18.769 --> 00:03:23.450
Butterfield has starred in several other young
adult-oriented movies, such as Miss Peregrine's

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:28.659
Home for Peculiar Children and The Space Between
Us, while Steinfeld is branching out in movies

00:03:28.659 --> 00:03:31.590
like the Pitch Perfect series and The Edge
of Seventeen.

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:34.849
It makes no sense to continue the series at
this stage.

00:03:34.849 --> 00:03:39.450
Then there are the bigger actors like Harrison
Ford, Ben Kingsley, and Viola Davis.

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:43.970
With Ford returning to his iconic characters
in recent years, he would be a difficult person

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:46.000
to nail down for the young adult sequel.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:50.189
To get all these people together again would
likely require more money than Lionsgate would

00:03:50.189 --> 00:03:51.930
be willing to cough up.

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:53.510
TV spinoff

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:57.950
Even if Lionsgate and the cast were to consider
a sequel, could the studio afford it?

00:03:57.950 --> 00:04:02.239
Hood made no secret about having difficulties
obtaining enough money for Ender's Game.

00:04:02.239 --> 00:04:07.200
If he was having trouble getting $110 million
in 2013, he's not going to be able to get

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:08.200
enough money now.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:12.830
And remember, there are several novels continuing
Ender's story, and even more in the Shadow

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:14.700
and Formic Wars series.

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:18.940
With so much material, the franchise could
work better as a television series instead

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:20.570
of a feature-film franchise.

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:23.060
Hey, it worked out pretty well for Game of
Thrones.

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:27.780
In fact, shortly after the movie released
in theaters, Variety reported that the studio

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:30.330
was considering a TV series spinoff instead
of a sequel.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:34.560
Since there were issues getting the necessary
money for the first movie and it didn't do

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:38.870
so well at the box office, it makes sense
for the studio to look at other options.

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:44.160
Unfortunately, there haven't been any updates
on the TV front since that report in 2013,

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:46.010
so who knows if it'll ever happen.

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:47.440
Thanks for watching!

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:50.450
